        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="mb-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold mb-1">How much does commercial lighting installation cost in Arlington, TX?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Commercial lighting installation in Arlington typically runs $3 to $12 per square foot, depending on fixture type, ceiling height, and whether you're doing new construction or a retrofit. A 10,000 sq ft warehouse LED retrofit averages $25,000–$45,000 including fixtures and labor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold mb-1">Are there utility rebates for LED lighting in Arlington, TX?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. Oncor Electric Delivery offers commercial rebates for qualifying LED upgrades in the Arlington area. Rebates typically range from $0.05 to $0.12 per kWh saved annually, and interior lighting retrofits can qualify for $25–$75 per fixture depending on wattage reduction.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold mb-1">Do I need a permit for commercial lighting installation in Arlington?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. The City of Arlington requires electrical permits for any commercial lighting installation or modification. All work must comply with the 2023 NEC as adopted by Texas. A licensed electrical contractor must pull the permit and schedule inspections.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-4">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold mb-1">How long does a commercial lighting retrofit take in Arlington?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Most commercial lighting retrofits in Arlington take 1–3 weeks depending on facility size. A 20,000 sq ft warehouse can typically be completed in 5–7 working days with a crew of 3–4 electricians, often scheduled during off-hours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-8">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold mb-1">What type of LED fixtures work best for Arlington's climate?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">For exterior applications in Arlington, you need fixtures rated for high-heat operation (ambient temps regularly exceed 100°F in summer). Look for LED drivers rated to 50°C or higher, and fixtures with IP65 or better ratings to handle severe thunderstorms. High-bay fixtures for warehouses should have a minimum L70 rating of 100,000 hours.</p>
        </div>

